well, actually it's not a patch, but a kernel module and iptables 
extension lib that build externally using kernel and iptables headers. 
this is my first code post to this list, and it's obviously not ready for 
anything official. I just want to get some response as to whether anyone 
is interested in further development.

this adds a match module called "throughput", which allows creation of 
named byte-rate throughput averages, which rules may contribute to and/or 
match against minimum/maximum bytes/sec. the throughput of each named 
average may also be read through /proc/net/ipt_throughput/<name>. I use an 
N-second sliding-window average over M-bucket algorithm for rate 
estimation that gives very good throughput estimates, with N and M both 
customizable through extra options to the iptables command when using -m 
throughput.

The attachment is a tar.bz2 of the source directory. Untar, cd to 
ipt_throughput/ and edit makefile to set the path to your iptables source 
directory, then run make and make install as root. Comments welcome.

- V. M. Condino

